---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Organization',
  name: 'Alan Estate',
  url: SITE.url,
  description: SITE.description,
  areaServed: 'AU',
};
---
<Base title="Alan Estate" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="container-x pt-16 pb-14 md:pt-24 md:pb-20">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_1fr] lg:items-end">
      <div class="max-w-2xl">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-5">When someone dies in Australia</p>
        <h1>You shouldn't have to work out what to do <em class="not-italic serif" style="font-style:italic">and</em> how to do it, at the same time.</h1>
        <p class="lede mt-6">Alan Estate is a free, step-by-step plan for the weeks and months after a death. Personalised to your state, the will, superannuation and any self-managed super fund. Written by people who have been the executor.</p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
          <a href="/guide/" class="btn btn-primary">Build your free plan</a>
          <a href="/guide/first-days/" class="btn btn-secondary">Just tell me the first steps</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-ink-3">No account. No payment. Nothing stored unless you ask us to email it to you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-paper relative overflow-hidden">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-4">A plan, not a pamphlet</p>
        <ol class="space-y-4">
          {[
            ['Now', 'Register the death, find the will, get certified copies'],
            ['First two weeks', 'Notify Centrelink, banks, super and the ATO'],
            ['First month', 'Work out whether you need probate in your state'],
            ['If there is an SMSF', 'ATO within 28 days, trustee structure within six months'],
            ['Months two to six', 'Find every asset, settle debts, hold before distributing'],
          ].map(([when, what], i) => (
            <li class="flex gap-4 items-start">
              <span class="num text-2xl leading-none w-8 shrink-0 pt-0.5">{i + 1}</span>
              <div><p class="font-semibold leading-snug">{when}</p><p class="text-ink-2 text-[0.95rem]">{what}</p></div>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why -->
  <section class="border-t border-line bg-paper-2">
    <div class="container-x py-16 md:py-20 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.3fr] lg:gap-16">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Why this exists</p>
        <h2>The will says who gets what. It doesn't say where anything is, or who to call.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose text-ink-2">
        <p>When one of us lost his father, the will was in the back of a filing cabinet at the farm, written thirty years earlier. The super was in a self-managed fund invested directly with a dozen managers, and the accountant's records were years out of date. There was a reverse mortgage nobody knew the terms of. The nomination for the super had lapsed years before, and nobody knew that either.</p>
        <p>Every institution wanted its own form, its own certified copies, and its own way of being told. Eighteen months later the estate was still open.</p>
        <p>None of that was unusual. It is what most Australian families walk into, with no map. Alan Estate is the map: the order of operations, what each step needs, who to contact, and where the traps are — starting with the free guide on this site.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What's in the guide -->
  <section class="container-x py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-10">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4">The free guide</p>
      <h2>Everything a first-time executor needs to know, in the order it happens.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-px bg-line border border-line rounded-lg overflow-hidden sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {[
        ['/guide/', 'Build your plan', 'Answer six questions and get a sequenced checklist for your situation — state, will, super, property, SMSF. Tick things off. Print it. Email it to yourself.'],
        ['/guide/first-days/', 'The first days', 'Who certifies the death, what the funeral director handles, where to look for the will, and what not to rush.'],
        ['/guide/certified-copies/', 'Certified copies', 'The most frustrating part of the whole process. Who can certify in your state, how many copies to get, and how to avoid doing it three times.'],
        ['/guide/who-to-notify/', 'Who to notify', 'Government, banks, super, insurers, utilities, subscriptions — and the free government service that tells many of them at once.'],
        ['/guide/finding-the-money/', 'Finding the money', 'Lost super, share registries, unclaimed money, managed funds, and what to do when the records are out of date.'],
        ['/guide/smsf/', 'When there is an SMSF', 'The deadlines that bite, what the surviving trustee must do, why the nomination matters, and how to wind the fund up.'],
      ].map(([href, title, desc]) => (
        <a href={href} class="bg-white p-6 md:p-7 no-underline group hover:bg-green-tint transition-colors">
          <h3 class="group-hover:text-green transition-colors">{title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-ink-2 text-[0.97rem]">{desc}</p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-green font-semibold text-sm">Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Two audiences -->
  <section class="border-t border-line">
    <div class="container-x py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mb-10">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-4">What we're building</p>
        <h2>The guide is free today. The product comes next.</h2>
        <p class="lede mt-4">Two tools that share one idea: the executor should never have to start from nothing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="card flex flex-col">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">For families</p>
          <h3>Your plan, your documents, one place</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2 flex-1">After a death: a personalised plan, drafted letters to every institution, and plain-English answers. Before: a simple record of where everything is — accounts, super, the nomination and its renewal date — with a handover to the people you choose when the time comes.</p>
          <a href="/families/" class="btn btn-secondary mt-6 self-start">See what's coming for families</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card flex flex-col">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">For professionals</p>
          <h3>Send families somewhere good</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2 flex-1">Funeral directors, aged care providers, SMSF accountants and advisers see the same gap every week: a family leaves the room with a folder and no idea what to do next. We're building the thing you can hand them — and, for SMSF practices, the nomination tracking that stops the worst case before it starts.</p>
          <a href="/professionals/" class="btn btn-secondary mt-6 self-start">See the founding partner pilot</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Principles -->
  <section class="border-t border-line bg-paper-2">
    <div class="container-x py-16 md:py-20 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
      {[
        ['General information, sourced', 'Every step links to the official source — the court, the ATO, Services Australia, your state registry. Where rules differ by state, we say so. Where we are not sure, we say that too.'],
        ['Unhurried by design', 'Most of this can wait until after the funeral. The plan tells you what genuinely cannot, and leaves the rest until you are ready.'],
        ['Nothing to sign up for', 'The guide runs in your browser. We do not store what you enter unless you ask us to email you a copy.'],
      ].map(([h, p]) => (
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-[1.2rem]">{h}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-ink-2">{p}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
